anagement\nCritical Care\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nRadiology\nSurgery\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\n24/7 ER and Specialty Care You Can Count On\nMedVet Vancouver is open 24 hours a day, seven days a week, 365 days a year providing exceptional emergency veterinary care for pets in Vancouver, WA, Clark County, and the area surrounding Portland, OR.\nOur expert team provides compassionate, comprehensive care for dogs and cats facing an emergency, injury, illness, or chronic condition. From the moment you walk through our door, your pet is our priority and we treat them like our own. We keep you informed every step of the way so you are a part of your pet’s care. We also partner with your family veterinarian as an extension of their practice so your beloved pet has a complete circle of care to give them the best chance for a long, healthy life.\nIf your pet needs emergency care, you can come directly to our hospital. No appointment is ever needed for emergency care, and our skilled team is here every hour of every day.\nMedVet Vancouver Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nCritical Care\nEmergency Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nRadiology\nSurgery\nOur Hospital Leaders\nJeffrey Barnet, VMD\nMedical Director\nBen Blood\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nAndreas Bachelez\n, DVM, DECVS, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nJeffrey Barnet\n, VMD\nEmergency Medicine\nEma M. Blumhagen\n, DVM, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nLauren Bracchi\n, DVM, DACVECC\nCritical Care, Emergency Medicine\nStephanie Byrne\n, DVM, MVetMed, Residency Trained in Veterinary Oncology\nMedical Oncology\nJoseph Cacioppo\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKristen Danielson\n, DVM, MBA\nEmergency Medicine\nSarah Depenbrock\n, DVM, MS, DACVIM (LAIM)\nEmergency Medicine\nJose Guerrero Cota\n, DVM, DACVR\nRadiology\nLydia Kazmar\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJamie King\n, DVM, MS, DACVIM (Neurology)\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nDan Krull\n, DVM, MS, DACVIM (Neurology)\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nChelsea Lemmon\n, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nInternal Medicine\nGrace Lim\n, BVM&S, MS, DACVAA\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nEmily Sachs\n, DVM, DACVECC\nEmergency Medicine, Critical Care\nAshley Sindelar\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nKatherine Spry\n, DVM, Residency Trained in Internal Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nDavid Sweeney\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJenn Thomsen\n, DVM, DPT\nEmergency Medicine\nAren VanLishout\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nJulia Wright\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMomo Yoshimura\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nShow All Doctors (\n22\n)\nPet Stories\n“\nWe’re so grateful to everyone at MedVet who helped our dog, Willow. She swallowed a latex glove whole! We’ve never been more impressed by their quick, friendly, compassionate care. Within five minutes, Willow was evaluated and given IV drugs to vomit the intact glove. We were back on the road within 45 minutes.”\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabi